  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\nA weakening mid level short wave will move east across our region \ntonight. Shower activity associated with this, currently back to our\nwest, will overspread our area this evening into the overnight hours\nbefore tapering off from the west later tonight. Given the weakening \nnature of the system, expect QPF amounts to be on the lighter side, \ngenerally around a quarter inch or less, with the highest amounts \nlikely across our southwest. \n\nLow level CAA will develop behind the front later tonight and into \nthe day on Monday. This will lead to much cooler temperatures with \nhighs on Monday only ranging from the mid 40s northwest to the low \n50s in the southeast.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2)\nThere is still a lot of uncertainty on exactly how the southern \nstream system lifting out of the southeast U.S. will interact and \nphase with additional mid/upper level energy dropping down from our \nnorthwest midweek. Overall though, it does look like pcpn associated \nwith this will develop up into our area through Thanksgiving day and \nlikely continue into Thursday night before tapering off heading into \nFriday. \n\nTemperatures will remain several degrees below normal with \ndaytime highs mostly in the 40s into next weekend. Ptype will be \nprimarily rain, but depending on how strong the northern stream \nsystem is and how much cooler air will be able to be pulled down into\nour area, at this point it's tough to rule out some wet snowflakes \nmixing in with the rain Thursday into Thursday night.",
